    "problemStatement": "You are given a function,\nint LeastDifference(int arr[], int length, int n);\nint LeastDifference(int arr[], int length, int n);\nstatic int LeastDifference(int[] arr, int n){}\nstatic int LeastDifference(int[] arr, int n){]\ndef LeastDifference(arr, n):\nThe function accepts an integer array 'arr' of size 'length' and an integer 'n' as its arguments.\nImplement the function to find and return the element of the array having least absolute difference\nwith the given number 'n'.\nAssumption: Only 1 integer will have least absolute difference.\nNote:\nn >= 0\nAbsolute difference means you have to ignore the sign of the difference",
